{"action":"revised","summary":"The filing gate reported one mechanical failure: the abstract was 152 words against the 150-word limit of 37 CFR 1.72(b). The abstract has been rewritten to 140 words (142 if the two hyphenated compounds are each counted as two words), so it passes under either counting rule with margin. No other section, claim, numeral, or figure brief needed a change, and none was made, so the numeral table, drawing descriptions, detailed description, claims, and all five figure files remain synchronized with one another and with the disclosure.","reasoning":["The overrun was small but the counter and my own whitespace count disagreed by two, which pointed at the hyphenated compounds cold-chain and phase-change being split by the gate's tokenizer. Trimming to exactly 150 by either measure would have left no margin against that ambiguity, so I cut to 140 whitespace words, which is 142 under hyphen splitting.","The words removed were redundancy, not technical content. The abstract still recites all four components, the suspended tray with its return passage and the two side supply passages, the spacer frame with two opposed cassettes and its inlet, guide ducts and peripheral outlets, the rib-into-channel registration that produces the outlet-to-passage overlap, and the full unpowered circulation path. Two savings came from merging the tray clause (the tray, whose side walls are spaced inward) and from tightening the closing path sentence.","I did not touch the claims, description, numeral table, or any figure brief. The gate raised no drawing, coverage, endpoint, or over-specification finding, and changing those files to chase a word-count failure would have risked desynchronizing text that currently agrees.","Re-verified after the edit that no placeholder, drafting note, or em dash exists anywhere in draft/ or figures/, and that every figure brief remains at or below the 2800-character limit."],"changes":["draft/10-abstract.md: rewritten to 140 words to satisfy 37 CFR 1.72(b), retaining the four components, the tray-suspension and side supply passage geometry, the spacer frame with two opposed phase-change cassettes and its inlet, guide ducts and peripheral outlets, the lid rib and mating channel registration producing outlet-to-passage overlap, and the complete passive circulation path."],"prior_art_strategy":"Unchanged from the prior turn, because no prior-art finding was raised. prior_art/INDEX.md still lists no references and the directory holds no reference files, so the draft contains no citations. Claim 1 continues to rest on the feature that a search is least likely to meet: the peripheral outlet openings must overlap the side supply passages for the path to exist, and that overlap is produced by the depending indexing rib entering the mating channel as the lid closes, in a carrier that has no fan, pump, or powered air mover. The specification states the problem that feature solves, namely that a module set down out of position silently defeats the circulation path with no outward sign. The dependent ladder retains its ordering by argumentative weight: gasket-after-registration sequencing, lid-loaded retention against transport lift, single-orientation keying, the condensate channel and wick chain, and the irreversible exposure indicator chain, with packing and depot servicing methods as separate statutory routes. The supplied art may be incomplete; claim 1 should be re-tested once a search is run.","questions":[],"answer":"The gate failed on one item only: the abstract ran to 152 words against the 150-word limit in 37 CFR 1.72(b).

**Fix.** `draft/10-abstract.md` is rewritten at 140 words. The gate's count and a plain whitespace count differed by two on the previous text, which indicates the two hyphenated compounds (`cold-chain`, `phase-change`) are each counted as two words, so the new abstract measures 142 under that stricter rule and still clears the limit with margin. The reduction came from redundancy: the tray clause is merged into a single relative construction, and the circulation sentence is tightened. All the substance is retained, namely the four components, the tray suspended over the return passage with two side supply passages, the spacer frame carrying two opposed phase-change cassettes with its central inlet, downward guide ducts and peripheral outlets, the rib-into-channel registration that produces the outlet-to-passage overlap, and the complete path travelled without a powered air mover.

**Everything else is untouched and remains synchronized.** No drawing, coverage, endpoint, or over-specification finding was raised, so the claims, detailed description, numeral table, drawing descriptions, and all five figure briefs are unchanged. Re-verified after the edit: no placeholders or drafting notes anywhere in `draft/` or `figures/`, no em dashes, all 30 numerals still defined once and used in the description, and every figure brief still at or below 2800 characters."}

